WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.892
This query keeps each completed admission.

00:00:02.892 --> 00:00:10.572
It calculates stay days for the admission and also calculates the patient's average stay using a window.

00:00:10.572 --> 00:00:15.027
The average is repeated beside each admission for that patient.

00:00:15.027 --> 00:00:21.347
This is useful when you need to compare an individual stay with the patient's usual pattern.

00:00:21.347 --> 00:00:27.372
Window functions preserve detail rows while calculating across a related set.

00:00:27.372 --> 00:00:30.987
PARTITION BY defines independent groups, ORDER BY defines sequence,

00:00:30.987 --> 00:00:36.702
and the frame defines which neighboring rows participate.

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:41.016
Those three choices are part of the business rule, not just syntax.
